    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 21 Giltspur Brook is an attractive and well-maintained three-bedroom semi-detached family home, ideally positioned within this mature, established and highly sought-after residential development.\n\nExtending to approximately 105 sq. m. (1,130 sq. ft.), this spacious property offers well-proportioned accommodation throughout and has been carefully maintained by its current owners. The property provides comfortable and versatile living accommodation, while the generous side area offers excellent potential to extend, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nUpon entering, the welcoming hallway leads to a bright and spacious living room, which benefits from a bay window overlooking the front of the property and offering lovely views towards the Sugarloaf Mountain. A gas fireplace provides a warm and inviting focal point, while double doors open through to the generous open-plan kitchen/dining room. This well-appointed space offers ample storage and provides an ideal setting for both everyday family living and entertaining. To the rear, a conservatory provides valuable additional living space and enjoys direct access to the private rear garden. Filled with natural light, this well-appointed space could be used as a second sitting room, dining area, playroom or a quiet reading space.\n\nUpstairs, the property offers three well-proportioned bedrooms, comprising two spacious double bedrooms and a versatile single bedroom. The principal bedroom benefits from an en-suite shower room and built-in wardrobes, while the second double bedroom also features built-in wardrobes. The third bedroom provides a flexible additional space and would could be used as a home office or a study making it an ideal option for those working from home. A family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation. There is also a large attic suitable for conversion. \n\nExternally, the property benefits from a neat front garden with off-street parking and a convenient side entrance. To the rear and a large private garden, providing an excellent outdoor space for relaxing and entertaining. A separate side patio enjoys excellent evening sunshine, creating a lovely area to sit out and enjoy the outdoors. The generous side space also offers excellent potential for extension, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nGiltspur Brook is a well-established and sought-after residential development located just off the Boghall Road in Bray. The location is particularly convenient, with Bray town centre and Bray DART Station within easy reach. A wide range of amenities are also available nearby, including Lidl, Aldi, Tesco and SuperValu, together with a selection of schools, shops, cafés, restaurants and leisure facilities.\n\nThe surrounding area offers plenty of opportunities to enjoy the outdoors, Killruddery House & Gardens, Shoreline Leisure Centre, Bray seafront and Bray Head are all within easy reach. The renowned Bray to Greystones Cliff Walk is also close by, offering one of the area's most popular coastal walks. The N11 and M50 are readily accessible, providing convenient links to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas.\n\nKey Features: \n\n• Attractive three-bedroom semi-detached family home in a well-established residential development\n• Spacious accommodation extending to approx. 105 sq. m. (1,130 sq. ft.)\n• Bright living room with bay window, Sugarloaf views and cosy gas fireplace\n• Generous open-plan kitchen, living and dining area with ample storage\n• Conservatory providing additional living space with direct garden access\n• Two spacious double bedrooms plus a well-proportioned third bedroom/home office\n• Principal bedroom with en-suite and built-in wardrobes; second bedroom also with built-in storage\n• Private rear garden with generous side access and potential to extend, subject to planning permission\n• Off-street parking, double-glazed windows, gas-fired central heating and security alarm\n• Excellent location close to Bray DART, town centre, seafront and local amenities, with easy N11/M50 access"
      },
